  - Consultations and public assessments followed, including inquiries in Sabah and
    Sarawak.
  - The Malaysia Agreement was signed on 9 July 1963 by Britain, Malaya, Singapore,
    Sabah and Sarawak.
  - Malaysia was formally established on 16 September 1963; Singapore later separated
    on 9 August 1965.
